# Bold Font Atlas and Size Granularity [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

> [SPEC:CXC-CYD-FONT-UNIFY] made the desktop and the CYD draw text from the SAME pre-rendered bitmap
> atlas, which collapsed the largest source of cross-tier pixel divergence. Two text defects survive it,
> and both are atlas COVERAGE gaps rather than renderer bugs: the atlas holds exactly one weight, so
> every `font_bold` request silently renders regular; and it holds no 6px or 7px entry, so the gauge
> tick labels and subtitles are rescaled 8→7 by nearest neighbour and arrive chunky. This spec closes
> both by widening the atlas — a second weight group and two smaller sizes — and changing nothing about
> the text rendering pipeline itself.

---

## 1. The defect

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-PROBLEM] Both surviving text defects are atlas coverage gaps, not renderer bugs

- definition: After [SPEC:CXC-CYD-FONT-UNIFY], two text-fidelity defects remain on the CYD. Neither is a
  fault in the glyph blitter — in both cases the renderer faithfully draws the best entry the atlas can
  offer, and the atlas has no better entry to offer.
- defect-weight: bold text renders as REGULAR on the CYD. The atlas carries one weight, and while the
  `font_bold` flag is stored on the canvas state it is never read at lookup time. Affected: the title
  "ComposeUX Dashboard" (14px bold) and the value readout "82.0 C" (12px bold).
- defect-scale: small text renders CHUNKY on the CYD. The requested size is ~7px, the nearest atlas
  entry is 8px, and the 8→7 nearest-neighbour downscale drops glyph rows unevenly. Affected: the gauge
  tick labels "40/80/120" and the gauge subtitle "Coolant Temp".
- consequence: the repair for both is the SAME repair — widen atlas coverage. Neither defect justifies a
  change to `draw_text`'s scaling arithmetic, and changing that arithmetic would break the pixel
  equivalence with the desktop that [SPEC:CXC-CYD-FONT-UNIFY] just established.
- invalidating-assumption: that the gauge subtitle's computed size stays at ~7.0px. If widget layout
  changes the derived font size, the exact-match size list must be re-derived from the layout rather
  than kept at 6/7.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

---

## 2. Atlas generator

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-GEN-WEIGHT] The generator takes a second face and emits two weight groups

- file: cyd/fonts/generate_atlas.py
- requirement: accept a `--bold-ttf <path>` flag naming the bold weight source. For a Helvetica TTC,
  the bold face is face index 1 in `/System/Library/Fonts/Helvetica.ttc`.
- fallback: when `--bold-ttf` is omitted, auto-detect the bold face inside a TTC collection by scanning
  for a FreeType `face.style_name` containing "Bold".
- output: generate two complete atlas sets — regular and bold — each at EVERY requested size, so the two
  groups are always symmetric and a weight lookup can never miss a size the other weight has.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-GEN-C] The C header gains a parallel bold lookup table

- file: cyd/src/font_atlas.h
- requirement: emit bold atlas structs alongside the regular ones, plus a parallel lookup array and a
  parallel find function, so firmware weight selection is a choice of TABLE and not a change of
  algorithm.
- symbols: `font_atlas_bold_<size>` structs; `font_atlases_bold[]`; `kNumFontAtlasesBold`;
  `font_atlas_find_bold(int target_size)`
- constraint: `font_atlas_find_bold()` MUST use the identical nearest-size search as `font_atlas_find()`
  — a divergence here reintroduces cross-weight scaling inconsistency.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-GEN-JSON] The JSON output gains a weight level above sizes

- file: python/composeio/render/font_atlas_data.json
- requirement: nest the existing per-size schema under two weight keys, `regular` and `bold`, each
  holding the `sizes` array the desktop loader already understands.
- constraint: both weight groups share the IDENTICAL per-size entry schema; the weight level adds a
  dictionary key and changes nothing below it.
- migration-note: this is a BREAKING shape change to the JSON contract — the top level was previously
  the `sizes` array itself. `BitmapFontAtlas.__init__` is the only reader and is updated in the same
  change ([CXC-CYD-BOLD-DESKTOP-CLASS]); the generator rewrites both outputs atomically, so a mixed-shape
  pair cannot be observed.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-GEN-SIZES] Two smaller sizes are added so small text needs no rescale at all

- requirement: extend the default size list from `8 10 12 14 16` to `6 7 8 10 12 14 16`.
- rationale-7px: an EXACT match for the gauge tick labels and subtitle text, which compute to ~7.0px.
  This eliminates the 8→7 nearest-neighbour rescale that produces the chunky rendering entirely, rather
  than making it look better.
- rationale-6px: coverage for very small annotations, so the smallest text in a scene is still an
  exact-size atlas hit rather than an upscale from the floor.
- cost: seven sizes across two weights is fourteen glyph sets; the flash consequence is budgeted in
  [CXC-CYD-BOLD-CYD-FLASH].
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

---

## 3. CYD firmware

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-CYD-SELECT] Firmware weight selection is a table choice, not a pipeline change

- file: cyd/src/canvas_esp32.cpp
- requirement: in both `draw_text()` and `measure_text()`, select the atlas by the canvas state's
  `font_bold` flag — `font_atlas_find_bold(target)` when set, `font_atlas_find(target)` otherwise.
- constraint: NOTHING else in the text rendering pipeline changes. Same scaling arithmetic, same
  blending, same alignment. Selection happens at lookup and the rest of the path is weight-blind.
- consequence: `measure_text()` must make the SAME weight choice as `draw_text()`, or measured advance
  widths will not match the glyphs actually drawn and alignment will drift.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-CYD-FLASH] The bold arrays must stay inside the flash budget

- requirement: verify CYD flash usage remains under 50% after the bold arrays are added.
- baseline: 24.8% flash used before this change.
- estimate: approximately 20KB additional for bold glyphs across seven sizes.
- verdict: well within budget; the check is a guard against a size-list mistake, not an expected risk.
- verify-machine: PlatformIO build output reports flash usage below 50% for the `cyd` environment.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

---

## 4. Desktop bitmap font

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-DESKTOP-CLASS] BitmapFontAtlas carries weight through every entry point

- file: python/composeio/render/bitmap_font.py
- requirement: `__init__` loads BOTH the `regular` and `bold` weight groups from the JSON atlas.
- requirement-lookup: `find_atlas(target_size, bold=False)` selects within the correct weight group.
- requirement-measure: `measure_text(text, font_size, bold=False)` passes the weight through to the
  lookup, so measurement and drawing agree on the tier the same way [CXC-CYD-BOLD-CYD-SELECT] requires
  on the firmware.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-DESKTOP-SKIA] SkiaCanvas records weight at set_font and forwards it

- file: python/composeio/render/skia_backend.py
- requirement: while the bitmap atlas is enabled, `set_font(family, size, weight)` records both the
  `size` and a derived `bold = (weight == "bold")`.
- requirement-forward: `draw_text()` and `measure_text()` pass that bold flag into `BitmapFontAtlas`.
- context: before this change the atlas had one weight, so `set_font` legitimately discarded `weight`
  ([SPEC:CXC-CYD-FONT-UNIFY] records that as intentional). This spec is what makes the discarded
  argument load-bearing again.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

---

## 5. Acceptance

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-VERIFY] The regeneration and verification sequence

- definition: the ordered post-implementation sequence that produces the evidence the compliance
  contract is judged against.
- verify-machine:
  - s1-regenerate: run `generate_atlas.py` with both weight sources and all seven sizes (6 7 8 10 12 14 16).
  - s2-crosscheck: run `cyd_dashboard_crosscheck.py` and save the atlas render to `cyd/screenshots/progression/`.
  - s3-build: build the CYD firmware and confirm flash usage is acceptable per [CXC-CYD-BOLD-CYD-FLASH].
  - s4-regression: run the existing font unification tests and confirm no regressions.
- verify-human: compare the new atlas render against the previous one on the glass — text specified bold
  must visibly carry heavier strokes, and "Coolant Temp" must read crisper at ~7px. Machine-green is
  necessary but not sufficient; weight and crispness are judged by eye, as in [CXC-LINE-TARGETS].
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

### [CXC-CYD-BOLD-COMPLIANCE] The compliance contract

- definition: seven acceptance criteria, each with the verification that settles it.

| ID | Requirement | Verification |
|----|-------------|-------------|
| BA-C1 | Atlas generator produces both regular and bold weight atlases | Inspect JSON: `regular` and `bold` keys both present with equal size count |
| BA-C2 | C header contains the bold lookup function `font_atlas_find_bold()` | Grep font_atlas.h for the function |
| BA-C3 | CYD draw_text uses the bold atlas when font_bold is true | Flash firmware, observe title "ComposeUX Dashboard" has bolder strokes |
| BA-C4 | Desktop bitmap atlas uses bold when weight is "bold" | Crosscheck PNG shows bolder title and value text |
| BA-C5 | The 7px atlas eliminates rescaling for gauge labels and ticks | Crosscheck: "Coolant Temp" renders crisper at ~7px |
| BA-C6 | Existing font unification tests pass | Test suite green |
| BA-C7 | CYD flash usage stays under 50% | PlatformIO build output |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-BOLD-ATLAS]

